<section class="hero">
  <h1>choudoufu</h1>
  <p class="tagline">Plenty of state. None of it binding.</p>
  <p class="tagline-sub">Your config says what should exist and the cloud says what does. No file gets a vote.</p>
</section>

<section class="lead">
  <p>choudoufu is OpenTofu with live resource markers. There is no state
  file, no backend and no lock. Ownership of a resource lives on the
  resource itself, as tags, and every plan rebuilds prior state from the
  live system instead of trusting a file. It is experimental and AWS only
  at the moment.</p>
  <p>Everything else in this fork is stock OpenTofu, unmodified. New here?
  Start with the <a href="faq.html">FAQ</a>.</p>
</section>

<section class="demo">
  <h2>See it work</h2>
  <p>One command runs the full demo against a local AWS emulator. It needs
  Docker. The exit code is the verdict.</p>
  <pre><code>bash stateless/e2e/run.sh --expect 5</code></pre>
</section>

